s":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan-review remediation for blocking G6 finding: clarified the plan to rename the stale MCP/CLI topic label to CLI exposure, retain positive CLI coverage, and add an explicit negative generator regression guard that fails if an MCP configuration-transparency/configuration-surface claim is restored. This preserves the approved documentation-only scope: no MCP tool and no runtime behavior change.","timestamp":1787418354392472001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Second plan-review remediation for blocking G1/G2 finding: the Plan now explicitly names `tests/unit/test_gen_config_reference.py` as the edit site for both the REQUIRED_TOPICS label correction and the negative regression assertion. It also pins the assertion to the unsupported `MCP config-transparency surface` phrase and equivalent MCP-configuration-surface wording. No historical parent, MCP inventory, or runtime behavior is added to scope.","timestamp":1787418904191559001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Third plan-review remediation for blocking T8 finding: enumerated both false generator assertions and their exact replacements. The Plan now changes the heading to `Exposure (CLI exposure)`, removes the `MCP config-transparency surface` clause, and makes the focused guard reject `MCP/CLI exposure`, `MCP config-transparency surface`, and `MCP configuration surface`. It also names the existing generator `--check` drift proof. Scope remains behavior-neutral with no MCP tool.","timestamp":1787419599801008001}],"created_at":1787417331713674001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Context\nThe generated configuration narrative says resolved configuration is exposed through an MCP configuration-transparency surface. Its adjacent heading also labels the topic as `MCP/CLI exposure`, although no MCP configuration tool exists. Both assertions originated in the accepted generator design on `consensual-ignored-ivorygull`.\n\n## Plan\n- In `scripts/gen_config_reference.py`, change the `Exposure (MCP/CLI exposure)` heading to `Exposure (CLI exposure)` and remove the `MCP config-transparency surface` clause so the paragraph describes only the implemented `rebar config` CLI view.\n- Retain accurate `rebar config` CLI exposure guidance.\n- Regenerate `docs/config-reference.md` and prove it is current with `python scripts/gen_config_reference.py --check`.\n- In `tests/unit/test_gen_config_reference.py`, rename the `REQUIRED_TOPICS` label from `mcp/cli exposure` to `cli exposure` while retaining positive coverage of the implemented CLI guidance.\n- In `tests/unit/test_gen_config_reference.py`, add an explicit negative assertion over the rendered configuration narrative that rejects each unsupported form: `MCP/CLI exposure`, `MCP config-transparency surface`, and `MCP configuration surface`.\n- Do not add an MCP tool or change configuration behavior.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The generated heading is `Exposure (CLI exposure)` and the paragraph contains no MCP configuration-surface claim.\n- [ ] Implemented CLI configuration inspection remains documented accurately.\n- [ ] `python scripts/gen_config_reference.py --check` proves `docs/config-reference.md` is current after regeneration.\n- [ ] Focused generator tests include the enumerated negative guard and fail on restoration of any removed MCP-exposure wording.\n- [ ] Configuration runtime and MCP tool inventory are unchanged.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"scripts/gen_config_reference.py","reason":"Remove unsupported MCP exposure narrative."},{"path":"docs/config-reference.md","reason":"Regenerate corrected configuration guidance."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gen_config_reference.py","reason":"Pin implemented exposure guidance."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["parent","66c6-2fe5-4850-4297"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"66c6-2fe5-4850-4297","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["documentation","f19a","configuration"],"ticket_id":"451a-c3c7-15fc-462a","ticket_type":"task","title":"F19A remove nonexistent MCP configuration exposure claim","verify_commands":[{"command":"python scripts/gen_config_reference.py --check","dd_id":"D1","dd_text":"Generated configuration reference is current"},{"command":"python -m pytest tests/unit/test_gen_config_reference.py -q","dd_id":"D2","dd_text":"Focused configuration generator contracts pass"},{"command":"make lint","dd_id":"D3","dd_text":"Generator lint passes"}]},"source_event_uuids":["ef924944-110a-425b-8603-c1c70a5d2472","f98925f1-6555-4ae2-aa8a-fd615b48c99e","d0ab23e4-38f0-4337-bed5-0efcd6465ed6","440144c5-0721-4d2e-9a30-e333ac0b426a","70178743-25f1-4921-aaaa-b366232774e9","3b0e7820-df78-4787-aa02-90bb374fbef8","5c642cbd-385b-453a-ba22-3cd4ac0e748c","c3d19e08-d36b-4993-aac0-25a6e79defdb","5c213ce9-dab7-46c0-9321-a5e40e8befc2","3f6cc81b-962f-4ee7-97b8-0da2662ec9d5"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787421916544783633,"uuid":"91463d55-2028-4f1d-aea4-21edfbee8e15"}